Q2: expansion to first order in fluctuations (with Galilean completion)
linear terms, given quadratic L :
    -rho_n*v_x*Derivative(u_x(t, x, y), t) - rho_n*v_y*Derivative(u_y(t, x, y), t) - rho_s*v_x*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), x) - rho_s*v_y*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), y) + (V*v_x - U(t, x, y))*drho(t, x, y)
linear terms, Galilean-completed:
    -rho_n*v_x*Derivative(u_x(t, x, y), t) - rho_n*v_y*Derivative(u_y(t, x, y), t) - rho_s*v_x*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), x) - rho_s*v_y*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), y) + (-rho_n - rho_s)*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), t) + (V*v_x - v_x**2/2 - v_y**2/2 - U(t, x, y))*drho(t, x, y)
completed - given: -rho_n*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), t) - rho_s*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), t) - v_x**2*drho(t, x, y)/2 - v_y**2*drho(t, x, y)/2
extra QUADRATIC terms from completion: -(v_x*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), x) + v_y*Derivative(phi(t, x, y), y))*drho(t, x, y)
coefficient of drho : V*v_x - v_x**2/2 - v_y**2/2 - U(t, x, y)    [= V.v - |v|^2/2 - U]
coeffs of (phi_x, phi_y, phi_t): [-rho_s*v_x, -rho_s*v_y, -rho_n - rho_s]   -> -rho_s v.grad(phi) - rho d_t phi
coeffs of (d_t u_x, d_t u_y): [-rho_n*v_x, -rho_n*v_y]   -> -rho_n v.d_t u
